// aeb build for Selenium Manager (the Rust CLI that manages browser/driver
// binaries for Selenium). This is the first tree migrated off Bazel to
// idiomatic aeb (see aether/BAZEL_TO_AEB_MIGRATION.md — the Rust pathfinder).
//
// Selenium Manager already ships a plain Cargo.toml + Cargo.lock; the old Bazel
// rust_binary/rust_library targets were thin wrappers over standard cargo. So
// the aeb build is: cargo build against the EXISTING manifest (never
// regenerate it) and publish the produced binary on the `cargo_binary` artifact
// edge for downstream consumers (the client bindings' Selenium Manager step).
//
// Toolchain: aeb selects whatever `cargo`/`rustc` is on PATH (rustc >= 1.85 for
// edition 2024). Bazel pinned the toolchain; this is the documented aeb
// divergence (PATH-selected, not hermetic).
import build
import rust
import rust (binary_name)

aeb(cap) {
    b = build.start()
    // Build the selenium-manager binary from the upstream Cargo.toml in this dir.
    rust.cargo_project_existing(b) {
        binary_name("selenium-manager")
    }
    return 0
}
